content.text:
Saved and tested:

```ts
getAppleMusicListeningHistory({
  date?: "YYYY-MM-DD",
  includeMetadata?: boolean,
  minObservedSeconds?: number
})
```

Examples:

```ts
// Today, with artist/album metadata
getAppleMusicListeningHistory()

// A particular day
getAppleMusicListeningHistory({ date: "2026-08-12" })

// Faster, without metadata lookups
getAppleMusicListeningHistory({
  date: "2026-08-12",
  includeMetadata: false
})

// Exclude very brief skips
getAppleMusicListeningHistory({
  date: "2026-08-12",
  minObservedSeconds: 30
})
```

It performs one streaming log scan, condenses events before returning, and batches metadata lookups in parallel. Validation for August 12 found **113 track starts across two sessions**.

I also added **`.pi/pit.json`** to enable project-scoped functions; Pi will recognize that setting on the next session reload.

arguments.code:
async () => {
  const history = await getAppleMusicListeningHistory({ includeMetadata: true });
  const grouped = new Map<string, { title: string; artist: string | null; album: string | null; plays: number; observedSeconds: number; firstTime: string }>();
  for (const track of history.tracks) {
    const key = `${track.title}\u0000${track.artist || ""}`;
    const current = grouped.get(key);
    if (current) {
      current.plays += 1;
      current.observedSeconds += track.observedSeconds;
    } else {
      grouped.set(key, { title: track.title, artist: track.artist, album: track.album, plays: 1, observedSeconds: track.observedSeconds, firstTime: track.time });
    }
  }
  const top = [...grouped.values()]
    .sort((a, b) => b.observedSeconds - a.observedSeconds || b.plays - a.plays)
    .slice(0, 10)
    .map((track, index) => ({ rank: index + 1, ...track, observedSeconds: Math.round(track.observedSeconds) }));
  return { date: history.date, timezone: history.timezone, trackStarts: history.trackStarts, sessions: history.sessions, top, note: history.note };
}

